      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Both UBI and expanded targeted welfare have potential trade-offs for ensuring long-term stability. UBI offers a broad safety net that could mitigate poverty nationwide and address job displacement from automation. Conversely, targeted welfare maintains more fiscal precision, potentially maximizing support for those with the most acute needs without the potential cost of a universal handout. The optimal path likely involves a hybrid approach that combines the broad stability of certain guaranteed income with strategic support for vulnerable populations.",
